{
  "id": "Compound::DB00155 - Gene::29943",
  "verbalization": "L-citrulline is implicated in the relationship with Padi1 through a series of interconnected molecular pathways. The evidence suggests that L-citrulline binds to Padi3, which is involved in protein citrullination, and Padi3 is also associated with Protein-arginine deiminase activity, which is a key enzyme in the citrullination process. This pathway is further linked to Padi1, indicating a potential functional dependency. The overlapping roles of Padi3 and Padi6 in mediating the same enzymatic activity suggest that L-citrulline may influence Padi1 through a shared mechanism involving protein citrullination. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for L-citrulline in modulating Padi1 activity, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
